# Trempel hub — the hub's layer of actions

Actions that don't depend on the engine's version: every project gets them. A user's
`~/.trempel/actions.mdz`, the project's kit and the project itself override any of them by id.

## actions

### open:folder
$title: Open folder
$icon: folder
$group: project
$js: actions/open.mjs

### open:ide
$title: Open in IDE
$icon: code
$group: project
$pin: true
$js: actions/ide.mjs

The editor command — `TREMPEL_IDE` (default `code`); a user's action `open:ide` replaces this one.

### terminal
$title: Terminal here
$icon: terminal
$group: project
$js: actions/terminal.mjs

### git:status
$title: Git status
$icon: git
$group: git
$when: git
$shell: git status --short --branch

### git:pull
$title: Git pull
$icon: download
$group: git
$when: $[git, git.upstream]
$shell: git pull --ff-only

### git:commit
$title: Commit everything
$icon: check
$group: git
$when: git.dirty
$input.message: { type: "text", label: "Message" }
$shell: $[git add -A ., git commit -m ${input.message}]

### kit:update
$title: Update the kit
$icon: arrow-up
$group: project
$when: dep:@trempel/kit
$input.version: { type: "text", default: "latest", label: "Version (or an npm spec)" }
$confirm: Changes package.json and the lock file, then runs the gates; roll back with git
$js: actions/kit-update.mjs

Raises `@trempel/kit` (and `@trempel/scene` to what that kit needs), then runs every gate of the
new kit (the `gates` group — tests, e2e, the YouTube build) and prints the result. Nothing is
committed: keep it — `git:commit`; roll back — `git checkout package.json package-lock.json && npm install`.
